{{wikipedia|dab=potter}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|British}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɒtə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-potter.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒtə(ɹ)}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|pottere}}, from late {{inh|en|ang|pottere||potter}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|pot|er}}, influenced by {{der|en|fro|potier||potter}}. More at [[pot]]. Displaced {{ncog|ang|crocwyrhta||crock-wright}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who makes [[pot]]s and other [[ceramic]] [[ware]]s.
#* '''1961''', J. A. Philip, "Mimesis in the ''Sophistês'' of Plato," ''Transactions and Proceedings of the American Philological Association'', vol. 92, p. 453,
#*: shoemakers, weavers, '''potters''', bronzeworkers who produced and purveyed the articles necessary for daily life.
# One who places flowers or other plants inside their pots.
# One who [[pot]]s [[meat]]s or other [[eatable]]s.
# One who [[hawk]]s [[crockery]] or [[earthenware]].
#* {{RQ:De Quincey Professor Wilson}}
#*:the convivial society of gipsies, tinkers, '''potters''', strolling players, &c.
# The {{vern|red-bellied terrapin}}, {{taxlink|Pseudemys rubriventris|species|ver=161005}} {{gloss|species of turtle}}.
# The [[chicken turtle]], {{taxlink|Deirochelys reticularia|species|ver=161005}}.

